-- title:
--   Special fibre of the strict transform of the ∞-component
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a Deligne–Rapoport model package $\mathfrak X$ for $p$, a discrete valuation domain $O$ whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $p$, an algebraically closed field $\kappa$ of characteristic $p$, and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$. Assume the site hypotheses [`V3Asm.SiteHyps`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSite.html#L267) (finiteness of the set of nodes, existence of oriented crossing charts over the base change of the Deligne–Rapoport model to $O$, the étale-neighbourhood data, injectivity of the assignment of node points and closedness of each such point, and the model hypotheses on $O$), and assume that each point $\xi_j$ lies in the open subset $X_0$ of the chart input, i.e. in the complement of the finitely many chosen node points. Write $Y$ for the glued resolved scheme, with its structure morphism $\mathrm{toBase} : Y \to \operatorname{Spec} O$ (the composite of $\mathrm{toDR}$ with the projection of the base-changed model to $\operatorname{Spec} O$). Then, for the ideal sheaf datum indexed by `Sum.inl 0` among the components, with associated closed immersion `subschemeι`, there is a morphism $e$ from the fibre product of that closed subscheme's structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} O$ with $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{to}\kappa)$ to the curve $(\mathfrak X.\mathrm{ratModel}\,\kappa).C$ such that $e$ is an isomorphism, $e$ followed by the structure morphism of $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{ratModel}\,\kappa$ equals the second projection, and $e$ followed by $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,\kappa$ and then by the base-change map [`ModularCurve.DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ`](def/ModularCurve_DRResolvedModelPackageV4.html#L24) equals the first projection followed by `subschemeι` and then by $\mathrm{toDR}$.
--
--   This identifies the geometric special fibre of the strict transform of the $\infty$-component in the resolved Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(p)$ with the corresponding rational model curve over $\kappa$, compatibly with the structure maps to $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa$ and with the projection to the base-changed Deligne–Rapoport model. It supplies one of the fields required by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageV4_and_dRResolvedModelCharts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageV4_and_dRResolvedModelCharts), which assembles the resolved model together with its étale crossing charts.
